{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>You shall not see your brother's ox.</b> Even at the time you go out to war. And it mentioned ox and donkey, and the same applies to all his livestock." "<b>And you would hide yourself from them.</b> Its Targum is ותתכביש, and לא תוכל להתעלם is translated לית לך רשו לכסיותה. Because והתעלמת speaks of an animal, to which the term covering does not apply, for a person is not made to hide it in his chest; rather the term suppressing the face applies. But regarding his garment, the term covering applies, for he can cover it with the corner of his garment. Another interpretation close to this: העלמה translated as כבישה — that is, in a case where it is in his domain." "<b>Returning you shall return them to your brother.</b> The verse repeated it (with both שב and תשיבם) on account of 'and if your brother is not near you and you do not know him.'"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:53:44.472551328Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}